# Line endings: LF in the index and in every checkout, Windows included.
#
# Git for Windows checks text out with CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true),
# and this repository holds text whose BYTES matter: the wudict howto is
# go:embed'ed from the worktree and its tests require a clean dump to reproduce
# it byte for byte, and the markdown golden files are compared with what the
# writer produces, which is LF. With CRLF checkouts those tests failed on
# Windows only, and a Windows-built binary would have shipped a guide that
# differs from everyone else's. Every text file in the index is already LF, so
# this changes no stored bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe misparses labels and GOTO in LF batch files; gradlew.bat uses both.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
